  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained short‑term oil price volatility increases transport and inventory risk premiums, incentivizing firms and governments to decentralize and regionalize production hubs (reducing geographic concentration of critical supply chains centered on a single country/region).</data>
