<edge source="sino_us_geoecon_rivalry::security_econ_policy" target="ai_infra_market_shift::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">When economic measures are explicitly justified by national security, governments institute additional review processes, export checks and licensing requirements that broaden and intensify oversight of AI activities.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">sino_us_geoecon_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_infra_market_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sino_us_geoecon_rivalry::security_econ_policy" target="cyber_critical_attacks::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">When economic policy is explicitly framed as national security, regulators receive broader mandates and political cover to increase inspections, audit demands, export controls enforcement, and sectoral oversight of firms and platforms.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">sino_us_geoecon_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">cyber_critical_attacks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sino_us_geoecon_rivalry::security_econ_policy" target="iran_gulf_escalation::kinetic_conflict_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Framing economic policy explicitly as national security (more sanctions, interdictions, and coercive economic measures) raises incentives for punitive responses by Iran and its proxies, producing more raids, strikes and escalatory kinetic actions in the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">sino_us_geoecon_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sino_us_geoecon_rivalry::security_econ_policy" target="russia_ukraine_war::negotiation_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Harder security‑framed economic policies produce stricter sanctions and conditionalities presented as non‑negotiable, reducing the political space and mutual incentive for Russia and Ukraine (and their backers) to engage in or sustain high‑tempo negotiated talks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">sino_us_geoecon_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
