<edge source="ai_infra_market_shift::ai_capital_inflow" target="cyber_critical_attacks::insider_compromise_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Surges in AI investment drive rapid hiring, contractor onboarding, and vendor proliferation (often with rushed access provisioning and weak segregation of duties), increasing the number of privileged accounts and opportunities for credential theft or insider collusion that raise insider compromise risk.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_infra_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">cyber_critical_attacks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_infra_market_shift::ai_capital_inflow" target="iran_gulf_escalation::diplomatic_activity_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained increases in AI investment into Gulf firms deepen commercial and security partnerships (joint ventures, on‑the‑ground programs), reducing immediate reliance on crisis shuttle diplomacy as economic linkage and private‑sector channels absorb routine coordination.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_infra_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_infra_market_shift::ai_capital_inflow" target="russia_ukraine_war::external_security_compet" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Larger private investment flows into AI firms—particularly in states aligned with or supplying technologies to Moscow—accelerate development of dual‑use surveillance and offensive tools, prompting rival powers to increase strategic pressure and competition around the Ukraine theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_infra_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_infra_market_shift::ai_capital_inflow" target="sino_us_geoecon_rivalry::domestic_tech_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Larger, sustained investment flows finance startups, local fabs, R&amp;D hiring, and supply‑chain development, directly expanding indigenous design and manufacturing capabilities for advanced semiconductors and AI hardware.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_infra_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">sino_us_geoecon_rivalry</data>
